{"duration_api_ms":1114697,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"957724d8-64ad-49ca-b532-5c5e66127a3c","total_cost_usd":46.050279499999995,"usage":{"input_tokens":462,"cache_creation_input_tokens":616002,"cache_read_input_tokens":71870908,"output_tokens":86021,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":22394},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":616002,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1679,"cache_read_input_tokens":472993,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1120,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1120},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":466,"outputTokens":86569,"thinkingTokens":22454,"cacheReadInputTokens":72006589,"cacheCreationInputTokens":788043,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":46.050279499999995,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":285,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The diff is fully printed above (in batches). Final report below.\n\n## 3. Uncertainty list\n\n- **F2/F4 (danmaku overlay)** — the overlay width formula assumes 3 items for live and non-file video danmaku (unchanged) and 1 for file sources. I did not run the UI, so the triangle offset for the narrow file-source overlay is only reasoned about, not seen.\n- **F3** — backoff is time-based (no timer), so a failed segment retries on the first position tick after the window. Also applies to explicit `queryDanmaku` calls on seek, which now respect the backoff.\n- **F6** — the shader is re-applied only when anime-ness *changes*; within one anime season the user's SR choice is kept. `Pref.superResolutionType` is re-read on the transition, so a change made on the previous anime page is picked up.\n- **F7** — `isManual: true` bypasses only the paused check; `isFileSource` still blocks all offline heartbeats, per the product rule.\n- **F9** — mute is an mpv-level mute. On mobile, unmute restores `Pref.playerVolume`, not the pre-mute mpv volume, since mpv is normally at that setting there. Hardware volume keys now clear the mute.\n- **F12** — I verified the plugin's single-static-listener behaviour in source, and the pop ordering (lower page rebuilds before the upper page is disposed) is reasoned from `didPopNext` setting `videoState`, not observed at runtime.\n- **F14** — this changes a base class used by most list pages: a refresh is no longer dropped while a load-more is in flight, so it now issues a request where it previously returned silently. Stale responses are dropped, including their `customHandleResponse` side effects (cursors). I checked the seven subclasses that touch `isLoading`; they guard their own entry points and are unaffected.\n- **F19** — I added a `like` field parsed as `int?` from `/x/article/viewinfo`. If the API ever returns a bool there, the cast throws. Note also that `Api.articleInfo` is *not* in `_accountApis`, so in incognito (and currently in login mode too) this flag will read 0; the fix removes the false positive but cannot show a true \"liked\" state until that endpoint is account-bound — that is a policy decision I did not make.\n- **F23** — **the biggest uncertainty.** `/x/space/acc/relation` (`be_relation`) is not verifiable offline, and this repo comments the WBI variant as 失效. If the endpoint is dead, `hasFollowedMe` returns null and 移除粉丝 stays hidden — the same as today, no regression. I also added it to `_accountApis`, which is required for the call to carry the account.\n- **F26 (fav \"search all folders\")** — I disabled the owner-only actions and the play-all context for `type == 1` rather than trying to resolve each result's real folder. That removes a real misuse of the wrong `mediaId`, but it also removes cancel-fav/copy/move from that specific search screen; if you'd rather keep them, the proper fix needs per-item folder data.\n- **F28** — the repost and like *counts* disappear with their buttons when not logged in; only the comment entry and its count remain. Keeping those two counts visible read-only would need new non-interactive labels, which looked like more than the finding asked for.\n- **F33** — the other watch-later tab is refreshed with a network `onReload` per delete (the pattern already used by 清空). It is correct but does cost a request.\n- **Shared files**: `lib/pages/login/controller.dart`, `lib/utils/accounts/login_policy.dart`, `lib/plugin/pl_player/controller.dart`, `lib/pages/video/controller.dart`, `lib/utils/self_test.dart` and `lib/common/widgets/dialog/export_import.dart` also contain the other fixer's pass-3 edits; the diffs above include both. In `export_import.dart` only the `dialogContext` rename is mine (the `beforeExport` parameter is theirs).\n\n## 4. TEST RESULTS\n\n```\nTEST RESULTS:\n  runner: flutter test\n  command: dart analyze lib test && flutter test\n  exit_code: 0\n  total: 102\n  passed: 102\n  failed: 0\n  skipped: 0\n  duration_ms: 2400\n\nINFRA REPAIRS (during auto-repair, empty if none):\n  (none)\n\nREAL FAILURES (audit-fix-caused regressions, empty if none):\n  (none)\n\nINFRA-PERSISTENT (failures that hit the 3-cycle repair cap, empty if none):\n  (none)\n\nOVERALL: PASS\n```\n\n`dart analyze lib test` reports 36 issues, all `info` level and all pre-existing in files I did not touch (vendored Flutter widget copies under `lib/common/widgets/flutter/` plus one in `vote_decoration.dart`). No errors or warnings. Every file I edited was run through `dart format`. I made no git mutations, and I left no temporary files behind.","ttft_ms":2628,"type":"result","duration_ms":1660885,"uuid":"4bbbf63b-71af-4c1b-a3f2-2230cf5b6f79","ttft_stream_ms":2265,"time_to_request_ms":571,"first_content_frame_ms":2265,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
